[00:00.00] On top of all smoking, all covered with snow
[00:12.00] I lost my two lovers, for courtings so slow
[00:19.00] For courtings of pleasure
[00:24.00] But parting is grief, and the false-hearted lover
[00:32.00] Is worse than a thief, a thief will just rob you
[00:41.00] Take what you have, but a false-hearted lover
[00:49.00] Will lead you to the grave, and the grave will decay you
[00:58.00] Turn you to dust, not one boy in a hundred
[01:06.00] A poor girl can trust, they'll hug you and kiss you
[01:15.00] Tell you more lies than frost-ties on a railroad
[01:23.00] Or stars in the sky
[01:45.00] So come all you young maidens
[02:06.00] And listen to me
[02:10.00] Never place your affection on a green willow tree
[02:18.00] For the leaves they will wither, roots they will die
[02:27.00] You'll all be forsaken, and never know why
